# Agent skills (pi)

This project uses the global agent-skills install. Pi auto-discovers skills from `~/.agents/skills/` — no config needed.

## Commands

Skills register as `/skill:<name>` commands (enabled by default):

```text
/skill:spec-driven-development add user authentication
/skill:planning-and-task-breakdown
/skill:incremental-implementation
/skill:test-driven-development
/skill:code-review-and-quality
/skill:code-simplification
/skill:shipping-and-launch
```

## Intent → skill mapping

Before non-trivial technical work, route to the matching skill:

| Intent | Skill |
|--------|-------|
| Feature / new functionality | `spec-driven-development`, then `incremental-implementation`, `test-driven-development` |
| Planning / breakdown | `planning-and-task-breakdown` |
| Bug / failure / unexpected behavior | `debugging-and-error-recovery` |
| Code review | `code-review-and-quality` |
| Refactoring / simplification | `code-simplification` |
| API or interface design | `api-and-interface-design` |
| UI work | `frontend-ui-engineering` |

## References

Checklists live at `~/.agents/references/` — open them when a skill points to them.

## Personas (optional specialists)

Personas live at `~/.agents/agents/`. Default to skills. Delegate to a persona when the user wants a dedicated specialist pass (review, security, test strategy, web perf audit). Personas do not call other personas; you (or the user) orchestrate.

| Persona | Prefer when |
|---------|-------------|
| `code-reviewer` | Full five-axis review before merge |
| `security-auditor` | Dedicated security / threat pass |
| `test-engineer` | Test strategy, coverage gaps |
| `web-performance-auditor` | Core Web Vitals / frontend perf audit |
